    "question": {
      ":question/id": "352b99ad-1edd-5fd4-84fe-58b9f240dd8b",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $N,$ given by\n\n$$\nN=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 5 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_{1}:=R_{1}+(-3)\\cdot R_{2}$ on $N?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation $R_{1}:=R_{1}+(-3)\\cdot R_{2}$ means that we need to add $-3$ times the second row to the first row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N &= \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 5 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{1}:=R_{1}+(-3)\\cdot R_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2+(-3)(6) & 2+(-3)(5) & 9+(-3)(-3) \\\\ 6 & 5 & -3\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-20 & -13 & 18 \\\\ 6 & 5 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
