      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-5 & -1 & -5 \\\\ -7 & 7 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_{2}:=R_{2}+(3)\\cdot R_{1}$ on $T?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation $R_{2}:=R_{2}+(3)\\cdot R_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T &= \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-5 & -1 & -5 \\\\ -7 & 7 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{2}:=R_{2}+(3)\\cdot R_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-5 & -1 & -5 \\\\ -7+(3)(-5) & 7+(3)(-1) & 1+(3)(-5)\\end{array}\\right] \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-5 & -1 & -5 \\\\ -22 & 4 & -14\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
